# Line endings, pinned, because this package is measured by bytes against a file that lives in
# another repository. `vendored/mcp_protocol.py` and `blender_ik_addon/mcp_protocol.py` have to be
# byte-identical — the suite digests one and compares it against the other, and the documents quote
# the revision that digest makes. A checkout that rewrote one copy's endings under the other would
# report a drift in the protocol that was never in the protocol, in the one check whose whole
# business is to say whether the protocol has drifted. The neighbours carry no such file, because
# none of them is measured against an other repository's working copy.
#
# Pinned here rather than left to `core.autocrlf`, which is `true` on this box: an attribute wins
# over that setting, and another party's global configuration is not mine to edit.
*                   text eol=lf
*.py                text eol=lf
*.md                text eol=lf
*.txt               text eol=lf
*.json              text eol=lf
.gitignore          text eol=lf
.gitattributes      text eol=lf

# What is not text is left strictly alone, whatever the guess about its first bytes.
*.dll               binary
*.pdb               binary
*.pyc               binary
*.png               binary
